# Network Model Register Specification

A network model is a relational mathematical model: it defines entities, relationships, directions, weights, pathways, diagnostics, boundaries, and process assumptions.

Required record fields: key, component_type, expression_or_structure, interpretation, review_question, and status.

High-priority review records include node definitions, edge meanings, edge weights, direction rules, centrality diagnostics, missing-edge assumptions, network boundaries, and process rules used for decision support.
